-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",149,{
[4737]="70020A66\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Grey Company.\n",
[4738]="70020A67\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred of the Grey Company.\n",
[4739]="7006D8FD\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive an Enedwaith barter currency allowance.\n",
[4740]="7003715B\n1\tTalk to Torferth in Tordag's encampment\tTorferth is at Tordag's encampment north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke. Tordag told you to lend your aid to his son, Torferth.\n2\tServants of the White Hand can be found at Torsbury and in the fields south of Torsbury. Torferth asked you to ride to Torsbury and the field to the south of the village and learn what kinds of forces are arrayed against his father's garrison.\t\n3\tTalk to Torferth at Tordag's encampment\tTorferth is at Tordag's encampment, north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke. You should return to Torferth with your report.\n",
[4741]="70047A86\n1\tDefeat enemies within Skoironk (total: 20)\tThe Enemy can be found within the caverns of Skoironk. You should defeat enemies within Skoironk.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many enemies within Skoironk.\n",
[4742]="70047AE3\n1\tDefeat enemies within the Towers of the Teeth (total: 20)\tYou should defeat enemies within the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many enemies within the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
[4743]="7002D3F2\n1\tDefeat goblins at Gazatmur (total: 10)\tGoblins can be found in Gazatmur, a large area in the east of the Great Delving. You should defeat many goblins at Gazatmur to thin their numbers.\n2\tReturn to Wigfast at his hiding spot\tWigfast is at his hiding spot near Gazatmur, the goblin-encampment of the eastern Great Delving. You should return to Wigfast now that you have thinned the goblins' ranks.\n",
[4744]="70046B22\n1\tSearch the Dome of Stars\030Search the House of Healing\030Search the Palace of Eldacar\030Find hidden supplies (total: 10)\tSearch interiors within after-battle Osgiliath for enemies and hidden supplies.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[4745]="70058BB6\n1\tDefeat enemies at Bagûd-mekhem (total: 30)\tEnemies can be found at Bagûd-mekhem. Foes loyal to both Gorgar the Ruthless and Hrímil Frost-heart have mustered at Bagûd-mekhem, the gate of winds. You should defeat them and aid the march on Gundabad.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a vast number of enemies at Bagûd-mekhem.\n",
[4746]="70058B85\n1\tDefeat the forces of Gundabad at Azgh-buzru (total: 30)\tGorgar's forces can be found throughout Azgh-buzru. You have encountered a vast number of Gorgar's forces at Azgh-buzru, the war-fell. You should defeat them and aid the march on Gundabad.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a vast number of the forces of Gundabad at Azgh-buzru.\n",
[4747]="7004AD13\n1\tDefeat enemies in Seregost (total: 15)\tMany threats can be found in Seregost's courtyards and terraces. You should defeat enemies in Seregost.\n",
[4748]="700469F0\n1\tDefeat Variags in the Firien Wood (total: 12)\tYou should defeat the Variags you find in the Firien Wood.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Variags in the Firien Wood.\n",
[4749]="700469F1\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Entwash (total: 12)\tYou should defeat the Orcs and Variags you find in the Mouths of Entwash.\n",
[4750]="7002C610\n1\tDefeat Ûngund Orcs near the site of the skirmish (total: 10)\tOrcs are likely to still wander the site of the skirmish near the slain hunter. You should defeat Orcs around the central hill of Thinglad.\n2\tReturn to Wynmar\tWynmar awaits you at his camp in the north-west of Thinglad. You should return to Wynmar with new of the many Orcs you defeated.\n",
[4751]="700173CD\n1\tComplete Avar's tasks in the Grand Stair\030Complete Pálmar's tasks in the Forges of Khazad-dûm\030Complete Teitur's tasks within Fil Gashan\tNarfi's brethren can be found at the Orc-Watch and Anazârmekhem, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall where Narfi holds his post. Narfi has asked you to visit his brothers, Avar, Pálmar, and Teitur at the Orc-watch and Anazârmekhem and learn what assistance they need.\n2\tTalk to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall\tNarfi is at the Twenty-first Hall, north-east of the Orc-watch and Anazârmekhem. After many difficult forays into the very heart of the Orc-strongholds of Moria, you have had decisive victories and thwarted the creatures' attempts to make a devastating blow upon the Elves of Lothlórien.\n",
[4752]="7000AF31\n1\tDeliver the haunches to Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn at the camp west of the Isendeep\030Collect Thistledown-haunches (total: 5)\tThistledown grazers are found on the southern side of the Hoarwell River or on the plains of the Steps of Gram. The grazing land near the Hoarwell is south and west from the dwarf camp and the grazing land in the Steps of Gram is to the south and east. Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that with some clever tactics, the Free Peoples may use the drakes against Angmar's host and sweep through the mines behind them to recover the position.\n2\tPlace the haunches on the flat stone near the War-tyrant\tThe flat stone is very near where the War-tyrant commands his forces within the Isendeep Mine. Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn wants to drive the forces of Angmar from the Isendeep. He believes with some clever placement, the Free Peoples may use the drakes against Angmar's host and sweep through the mines behind them to recover the position.\n",
[4753]="70033304\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Sudulthurkh (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found pushing mine-carts at the cross-roads of Sudulthurkh in Nud-melek, north of the great chasm. You should defeat the war-mongering Orcs of Moria before they can wreak havoc upon the Dale.\n2\tReturn to Svanr at Sudulthurkh\tSvanr can be found in a corner of the path just east of Sudulthurkh. You should speak with Svanr.\n",
[4754]="7002D459\n1\tFind Stíling at Gamil Filik\tStíling is scouting the outskirts of Gamil Filik in the Silvertine Lodes, south and then slightly east of the Deep Descent. You should speak with Stíling and offer your services against the goblin threat.\n",
[4755]="700071A1\n1\tDeliver the Dourhand medallion to Refr Quicksilver\030Collect the Dourhand Overseer's medallion\tThe overseer of the Dourhands may be found within the ruins of Mithrenost, south of Refr Quicklsilver. Refr Quicksilver has asked to seek out and defeat the overseer of the Dourhands at Mithrenost, in hopes that his followers will turn from their evil ways. He asked you to bring him evidence of the overseer's defeat.\n",
[4756]="700334FB\n1\tDefeat enemies and monsters in the Second Hall (total: 8)\tEnemies and vile creatures can be found in the Second Hall of Nud-melek. You should defeat enemies in the Second Hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of enemies in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.\n",
[4757]="70058CED\n1\tDefeat Gorgar's forces at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (total: 18)\tThe forces of Gorgar the Ruthless can be found in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh, Orc-encampments that straddle the gates of Mount Gundabad. Countless numbers of Orcs, trolls, and goblins loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless inhabit Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should defeat as many as you can to aid the Gabil'akkâ in reclaiming Mount Gundabad.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a significant number of Gorgar's forces at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\n",
[4758]="70062151\n1\tCollect diseased boar meat (total: 10)\tMerruth has asked you to hunt diseased boars in eastern Cardolan, and to place the meat along the route to the Warg dens nearby.\n2\tBring the meat to Merruth\tYou should bring Merruth the diseased meat. Merruth is in eastern Cardolan.\n",
[4759]="7001A4B0\n1\tTalk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd\030Talk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion\tGlamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, south-east from Echad Sirion, at the southern foot of Amon Angened. Aemeldir is at Echad Sirion. Farasgon has asked you to speak with Glamodúd regarding the Orc-camp to the south and Aemeldir regarding Dúrburz-stazg, the encampment to the north.\n",
[4760]="7005AABF\n1\tCollect the first hobgoblin report\030Collect the second hobgoblin report\030Collect the third hobgoblin report\030Collect the fourth hobgoblin report\030Collect the fifth hobgoblin report\tScraps of paper inside the out-camp might hold information intended for the hobgoblin leadership... but they might be intercepted by a daring adventurer.\n2\tTalk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag\tKlúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.\n",
[4761]="70043DFC\n1\tSlaughter members of the Gondorian Army at the Armoury (total: 10)\tThe Armoury is located on the Western side of Osgiliath. You should fight and slaughter foes around the Armoury.\n2\tListen to Grazadhal yell at you\tGrazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth. You should listen to Grazadhal yell at you.\n",
[4762]="70043DED\n1\tDefeat minions of Mordor at the Eastern Wharf (total: 10)\tThe Eastern Wharf is located on the Eastern side of Osgiliath. You should fight and slaughter foes around the Eastern Wharf.\n2\tSpeak with Melethon\tMelethon is at the Causeway Forts. You should speak to Melethon.\n",
[4763]="7000004F\n1\tAdd foul-smelling draught to goblin food-barrels (quantity: see journal)\tThere will be barrels of uneaten food at the goblin-camps of Weatherfoot, north-east of The Forsaken Inn and south-west of Weathertop. Lieva Dourlily has asked you to take a special draught she brewed to the goblin-camps in the north-east and introduce it into their food supply. The draught is supposed to have properties that Lieva thinks will encourage the goblins to abandon the Lone-lands.\n2\tTalk to Lieva Dourlilly at The Forsaken Inn\tLieva Dourlily awaits your return at The Forsaken Inn, south-west of Weatherfoot. You added the contents of Lieva's draught to the food-barrels found at the goblin-encampments north-east of The Forsaken Inn. Lieva will want to know of your success.\n",
[4764]="7001CC64\n1\tDefeat servants of the Enemy at Durbúrz-stazg (total: 15)\tDurbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Aemeldir has asked you to defeat servants of the Enemy at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.\n2\tTalk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion\tEchad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg. You should return to Aemeldir with news of your success.\n",
[4765]="70058B87\n1\tDestroy Orkish ballistae at Azgh-buzru (total: 10)\030Destroy Orkish trebuchets at Azgh-buzru (total: 8)\tOrkish trebuchets and ballistae can be found at Azgh-buzru. Órug has asked you to destroy trebuchets and ballistae at Azgh-buzru.\n2\tTalk to Órug at Drenghól\tÓrug can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. You have destroyed many trebuchets and ballistae at Azgh-buzru. You should report to Órug at Drenghól.\n",
[4766]="70059B64\n1\tDeliver 50 Host of the West Silver Pieces to the Host of the West Quartermaster\tThe Host of the West Quartermaster asked you to bring them fifty Host of the West Silver Pieces.\n",
[4767]="70059B66\n1\tDeliver 100 Host of the West Silver Pieces to the Host of the West Quartermaster\tThe Host of the West Quartermaster asked you to bring them one-hundred Host of the West Silver Pieces.\n",
[4768]="70072517\n1\tSpeak with Irsinith at the Mother Tree\tViznak wants you to bring the tale and news of the king's story to Irsinith, the Warden of the Mother Tree in Adagím.\n2\tPresent your story to Ildimár at Sul Madásh\tIrsinith, inspired by your story, will commune with the Mother Tree. While she does, she asks that you visit her father and mother at Sul Madásh.\n3\tHear Dáthlil's response to your story\tIrsinith, inspired by your story, will commune with the Mother Tree. You have spoken with Irsinith's father. He asked that you speak with her mother before returning to Irsinith at the Mother Tree.\n4\tReturn to Irsinith at the Mother Tree and see what she learned\tYou learned some more about the blight from Ildimár and Dáthlil, return to Irsinith at the Mother Tree in Adagím and see what she learned from her communion with the ancient tree.\n",
})
